  "$comment": "#FEED-191 (owner 2026-11-04). THE RESULTS TAB ×4: the session screen's strip ends with ONE `tab.copy.label` tab, pinned right (every host draws it after the last chip; phones icon-only like Conversation, the concept `chat-results`, md+/IDE icon + label; a page of the phones' pager, the last one; no dot). A RESULT = a session's OWN `surface` card (`messages` row with author_session_id = session_id, no engine `questionId`) with `card.result` true; `card.result` absent reads the older `card.story`; both absent = any RESOLVED picture (attachmentId set) makes it one (`isResultCard`). A plan or a question is NEVER a result: plans live on the Plan tab (plan-page.json), waiting ones in Needs you (needs-you.json). `exponential_show {pictures, description, result?}` writes them: pictures default to a result, a plain surface (a status card) stays in the chat; `result: false` keeps pictures in the chat only. FOLD `resultsTab({now, rootId, sessions, messages})` (messages = the root's session-authored card rows, root_id + author_session_id + card, sealed ones opened; never a chat's loaded window, #EXP-1380; the tab's count folds the same) (every mirror replays `cases`, comparing the WHOLE array): every result of the root's tree (session.rootId = rootId), never expiring, NEWEST first (createdAt desc, then id desc); no replacing: a newer result never hides an older one. A RESULT (out): id, sessionId, sessionName, createdAt, age (`<m>m` under an hour, `<h>h` under a day, else `<d>d`, floored; under a minute `copy.now`), title (the card's title trimmed; blank = `copy.untitled`), description (trimmed; blank = null), pictures (the RESOLVED ones in card order {label, attachmentId, width, height, caption}), surface (the card has one). BODY (top to bottom, ONE scroll, centred column like the conversation): (1) the PR block while session-chat.json `guidePullRequest` is set: in a linear open stack the `tab.copy.stack` band + THE StackRail, then ONE `tab.copy.changes` row (the diff glyph, `+a −d · n files` from THE DiffCounts) opening THE review pane (its back row reads `‹ tab.copy.label`); no PR = no block. (2) `tile.leadGap` under the PR block, the results INLINE, `tile.listGap` apart: a SECTION = line 1 the title (semibold medium, one line, truncated) with `age` muted at the trailing end, NO badge; then the description (muted, wrapping) `tile.textGap` under it; then, `tile.gap` under that: pictures win: ONE horizontal row of THUMBNAILS (each `tile.thumbHeight` tall, width by aspect capped at `tile.thumbMaxWidth`, an unknown size = 4:3; `tile.radius`, `tile.gap` apart, the glass-stroke hairline; scrolls sideways past the column) with ONE muted line under each = the caption, else the label; else a surface = THE surface renderer inline (chats.json `surfaceCard`'s tree, the column's width, no title over it; presses behave as in the chat). A press on a picture opens THE lightbox (`ImagePreviewDialog` + guide-viewer `‹ i / n ›`) over that result's pictures at its index; nothing else presses. (3) no result = THE EmptyState (`tab.copy.empty`, the concept `chat-results`, no subtitle); the PR block still shows above it. Styleguide `results-tab` (Exponential-specific, not eUI) draws `tab.specimen` wide and phone. An older deep link `?tab=stories` (and `?tab=guide`) lands on `?tab=results`. PR PICTURES (`isPrPictureCard`, TS only, `prPictureCases`: the server's PR body, pr-body.json, and the `pr open` guard): the resolved pictures of a session's own result, plan or question card; `result`/`story` false keeps a card out. Mirrors: desktop domain::results_tab, iOS ExpCore ResultsTab.swift, Android domain/ResultsTab.kt.",
